# ==============================================================================
# cloud-design .gitignore
# ==============================================================================
# Purpose: keep machine-local, regenerable and secret-bearing files out of git.
#
# RESOLVED. This banner used to warn that `terraform/.terraform` (~711 MB of
# provider binaries) and three `__pycache__` directories were still TRACKED, and
# to instruct a maintainer to run `git rm -r --cached` on them by hand. That
# remediation was done in commit 8c7a65f, so the warning was stale: it told the
# next person to untrack paths that were no longer tracked.
#
# Verify with:  git ls-files | grep -E '\.terraform/|__pycache__|\.pyc'
# That command must print nothing. If it prints something, the ignore rules below
# are not the problem -- the file is tracked and needs `git rm --cached`.
#
# This is deliberately NOT run by scripts/ -- removing files from the index is a
# git write, and this repository is being edited concurrently by other teams.
# ==============================================================================

# --- Terraform: state, plans and the provider cache -------------------------
# terraform.tfstate contains resource IDs and often secrets-adjacent values.
terraform/.terraform/
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
terraform/terraform.tfstate
terraform/terraform.tfstate.*
terraform/terraform.tfstate.backup
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.tfvars
!terraform/terraform.tfvars.example
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.*
tfplan
tfplan.*
override.tf
override_*.tf
*_override.tf
*_override.tf

# --- Secrets: real credentials must never be committed ----------------------
# NOTE: .env.example is deliberately NOT ignored -- it is the committed template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# --- Generated docs assets --------------------------------------------------
docs/resources/

# --- Logs -------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/

# --- Editor / OS cruft ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.bak
*.orig
.idea/
.vscode/
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project